  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(I) <math><mn>1</mn><mo>°</mo></math> allylic halide have less steric hindrance, so it is more reactive for <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></math> reaction.<br />(III) <math><mn>3</mn><mo>°</mo></math> allylic halide gives most stable tertiary allylic carbonium ion so most reactive towards <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> reaction.",
